=== 1. Shadow-fill fault handling vs vCPU count ===
  512 private 4 KB pages/vCPU/round, 300 rounds, group of 16 pages per sample.
  Touched bytes per vCPU per round: 65536 B of data (one 8 B load per page) + a 4 KB
  shadow L3 + 16 KB of x86 tables -> ~84 KiB of live cache lines per vCPU.

  -- page tables: PRIVATE per vCPU (own root, own tables, own pages)
  Each N is bracketed by a freshly measured N=1 run so DVFS/background drift
  cannot masquerade as scaling; 'solo' is that adjacent N=1 figure.
    N   solo ns    p50 ns     worst    p99 ns  vs solo agg faults/s    eff    ovl
    1    158.85    171.88    171.88    200.52   1.082x         5.82M    92%   1.00
    2    174.48    174.48    174.48    213.54   1.000x        11.46M   100%   0.99
    4    171.88    187.50    187.50    223.96   1.091x        22.13M    95%   0.95
    6    169.27    184.90    187.50    223.96   1.092x        33.10M    93%   0.93
    8    166.67    182.29    187.50    531.25   1.094x        44.31M    92%   0.78

  -- page tables: SHARED root (one TTBR0/ASID for all vCPUs, shared L0/L1/L2, private L3 + private pages)
  Each N is bracketed by a freshly measured N=1 run so DVFS/background drift
  cannot masquerade as scaling; 'solo' is that adjacent N=1 figure.
    N   solo ns    p50 ns     worst    p99 ns  vs solo agg faults/s    eff    ovl
    1    166.67    171.88    171.88    200.52   1.031x         5.82M    97%   1.00
    2    179.69    169.27    169.27    651.04   0.942x        11.82M   106%   0.95
    4    174.48    184.90    184.90    562.50   1.060x        22.28M    97%   0.91
    6    174.48    187.50    190.10    520.83   1.075x        32.80M    95%   0.88
